-- title:
--   Common level-stable finite-type chart dominated by all ends
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $N=q\ell$, $C=\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\;A\;K\;j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, $\mathfrak X=\mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel}\;A\;K\;j$ for the two-chart integral model (the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras along the middle chart), and $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ for its stalks. For a matrix $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and an $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$, the predicate $\mathtt{IsLevelAutAt}\;L\;N\;\xi\;N\;(N^2M')\;(\mathtt{levelH}\;N\;M')\;\gamma^{-1}\;K\;\tau$ asserts that $\tau$ realises the slash action of the matrix attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ at width $N$: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, $g$ having nonzero series, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the quotient of those series, and every embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=e^{2\pi i/N}$, one has $\iota\bigl((\tau x)\bigr)\cdot q\text{-}\exp\bigl(g\mid_k\mathtt{conjElemN}\,N\,\gamma\bigr)=q\text{-}\exp\bigl(f\mid_k\mathtt{conjElemN}\,N\,\gamma\bigr)$; such a $\tau$ is called below a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   The data are: primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge3$ with $\ell\neq q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic $0$; a primitive $N$-th root of unity $\xi\in L$; the hypothesis `hι`, that some ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/N}$; an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq L((t))$ with `hK`, that $K$ is the $L$-span (in the sense of $\mathtt{laurentBaseChange}$, the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image) of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H(N^2M')$, where $H=\mathtt{levelH}\;N\;M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/N)^\times$; a henselian discrete valuation ring $A$ which is an $A$-algebra domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), together with compatible $A$-algebra structures on $L$ and on $K$; an element $j\in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $j$-series $\mathtt{jq}$ (`hj`); a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ (`hϖ`); and a tame element $\varpi_t\in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Next, a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathtt{ssJSet}\;q\;\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the rigidified Drinfeld-chart package at all supersingular points of the model: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that the image $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ under $A\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of the affine chart $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ whose ideal satisfies the supersingularity condition of `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv\mathtt{drinfeldForm}\;q\;W=X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and an isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $\mathcal S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map to the completion and $\mathrm{germY}\colon C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ for the germ map through the chart: (i) $e$ takes the image of $a\in A$ to the constant $\sigma a$; (ii) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ such an automorphism induces the identity on $C/y'$; (iv) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and inducing the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $\mathcal S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with $\theta\circ e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}=e\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}\circ\tau|_C$, with $\theta$ fixing constants, with $\theta(X_{j_0})\equiv\sum_{i}M_{ij_0}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, with $c^{q+1}\equiv1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, with $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and with $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $\mathcal S$, each omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, each containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ and $a_i,b_i\in\mathbb Z$, have distinct contractions to the stalk as soon as $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$; (vi) for such a prime $P$ with direction $(1:0)$, an element $a\in C$ has its germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) the rescaled $j$-series $\mathtt{jqNModC}\;L\;N$ lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with that element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i\le e_0}(\text{coeff of }X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}\text{ in }h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, such that $e$ of the germ of that element minus $a_0$ is the class of $h$.
--
--   There are then fixed: a point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ with $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of its stalk, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`), and one such chart witness $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ at $z$, with $\mathcal S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$, whose seven clauses (i)–(vii) above are assumed in `hW₁` for this witness.
--
--   Further data and hypotheses: an ideal $J$ of $C$ with `hJ`, that $J$ is the infimum, over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, of the preimage under $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $\mathcal S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$; an $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ with `hB`, that $B$ is generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$; a valuation subring $W$ of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`); the hypothesis `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W\cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ precisely when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the elements outside $\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), requiring: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ a surjection $\rho\colon B\to\mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\;q\;k$ with kernel $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W$, through an element $(\mathtt{redQ}\;q\;\gamma,c)$ of $\mathtt{hSubgroup}\;q$ acting by $\mathtt{hAction}$, with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; that the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached by translating $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$ by some level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally: a finite set $\mathtt{ends}$ of subrings of $K$ characterised by `hends`, namely $O\in\mathtt{ends}$ if and only if there are $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of the $A$-subalgebra $B_a$ generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\ xa\in J\}$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ inside $K$ (that is, $f\in O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$), every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$, and $B\not\subseteq O$; the hypothesis `hperm`, that for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, each $O\in\mathtt{ends}$ is carried to some $O'\in\mathtt{ends}$ in the sense that $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$; and an invariant section, namely $n\in\mathbb N$ and $S\in C$ with `hS`: $n\ge1$, $S\in J^n$, $S\neq0$ in $K$, $S$ is fixed by every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, and for every $O\in\mathtt{ends}$ and every $i\in J^n$ the quotient $i/S$ lies in $O$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of an $A$-subalgebra $B_c$ of $K$ with the following three properties. First, $B_c$ is of finite type over $A$. Second, $B_c$ is stable under the deep level automorphisms: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\tau$ maps $B_c$ into $B_c$. Third, every $O\in\mathtt{ends}$ contains $B_c$ and is the localisation of $B_c$ at those of its elements that become units: $f\in O$ if and only if there are $g,h\in K$ with $g\in B_c$, $h\in B_c$, $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$, and $fh=g$.
--
--   This is the second half of the construction of a single level-stable affine chart of finite type over $A$ dominated by all the ends of the blown-up supersingular chart of the integral model: it converts an invariant section $(n,S)$ of $J^n$, produced in the first half, into the common chart $B_c$ together with the description of each end as a localisation of $B_c$. It feeds the assembled statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_commonChart_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), which is used in the analysis of the special fibre of the model at the supersingular points and of the action of the level automorphisms on it.
